      "file": "gas_dehydration_unit_temperature.glb",
      "title": "Absorption at high pressure, regeneration at high temperature",
      "description": "In the contactor wet gas (often 30–100 bar) rises through trays while lean triethylene glycol (TEG, typically ~ 98.5–99.9 wt %) absorbs its water. Rich glycol is flashed, heated and boiled in the reboiler at about 200 °C (below TEG decomposition ~ 206 °C) to drive the water off through the still. Typical outlet water content ≈ 7 lb/MMscf (~ 110 mg/Sm³) pipeline specification.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
