  "summary": "A TEG gas dehydration unit removes water vapour from natural gas so it does not form hydrates or corrode pipelines. In the contactor, wet gas rises through trays against a downflow of lean triethylene glycol, which absorbs the water. The rich glycol is regenerated by boiling off the water in a reboiler and returned.",
